                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3d1c26ff-7b55-414d-bdd0-e433b745cc5e",
                                "sense_id": "84bcfa8b-f048-3119-aa7f-6ebf7277a6b7",
                                "text": "Le panslavisme a été défini par un idéologue croate Vinko Pribojević au XVe siècle, repris par un missionnaire croate Juraj Križanić (Yuri Krijanich) au XVIIe siècle et surtout développé par le philosophe russe N. I. Danilevski (1822-1885).",
                                "translation": "Pan-Slavism was first described by a Croatian ideologist, Vinko Pribojević, in the fifteenth century, revived by a Croatian missionary, Juraj Križanić (Yuriy Krizhanich), in the seventeenth century, and above all developed by the Russian philosopher N. Y. Danilevsky (1822–1885).",
                                "english": "Pan-Slavism was first described by a Croatian ideologist, Vinko Pribojević, in the fifteenth century, revived by a Croatian missionary, Juraj Križanić (Yuriy Krizhanich), in the seventeenth century, and above all developed by the Russian philosopher N. Y. Danilevsky (1822–1885)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
